{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":25,"code":"LAM","name":"Lamentations","testament":"OT"},"chapter":5,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"LAM 5:1"},"Remember, O LORD, what is come upon us: consider, and behold our reproach. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:1"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"LAM 5:2"},"Our inheritance is turned to strangers, our houses to aliens. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:2"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"LAM 5:3"},"We are orphans and fatherless, our mothers ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," as widows. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:3"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"LAM 5:4"},"We have drunken our water for money; our wood is sold unto us. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:4"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"LAM 5:5"},"Our necks ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["are"]}," under persecution: we labour, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and "]},"have no rest. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:5"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"LAM 5:6"},"We have given the hand ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["to"]}," the Egyptians, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and to "]},"the Assyrians, to be satisfied with bread. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:6"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"LAM 5:7"},"Our fathers have sinned, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and are"]}," not; and we have borne their iniquities. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:7"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"LAM 5:8"},"Servants have ruled over us: ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["there is"]}," none that doth deliver ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["us"]}," out of their hand. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:8"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"LAM 5:9"},"We gat our bread with ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["the peril of"]}," our lives because of the sword of the wilderness. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:9"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"LAM 5:10"},"Our skin was black like an oven because of the terrible famine. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:10"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"11","sid":"LAM 5:11"},"They ravished the women in Zion, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," the maids in the cities of Judah. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:11"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"12","sid":"LAM 5:12"},"Princes are hanged up by their hand: the faces of elders were not honoured. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:12"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"13","sid":"LAM 5:13"},"They took the young men to grind, and the children fell under the wood. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:13"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"14","sid":"LAM 5:14"},"The elders have ceased from the gate, the young men from their musick. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:14"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"15","sid":"LAM 5:15"},"The joy of our heart is ceased; our dance is turned into mourning. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:15"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"16","sid":"LAM 5:16"},"The crown is fallen ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["from"]}," our head: woe unto us, that we have sinned! ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:16"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"17","sid":"LAM 5:17"},"For this our heart is faint; for these ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["things"]}," our eyes are dim. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:17"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"18","sid":"LAM 5:18"},"Because of the mountain of Zion, which is desolate, the foxes walk upon it. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:18"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"19","sid":"LAM 5:19"},"Thou, O LORD, remainest for ever; thy throne from generation to generation. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:19"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"20","sid":"LAM 5:20"},"Wherefore dost thou forget us for ever, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," forsake us so long time? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:20"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"21","sid":"LAM 5:21"},"Turn thou us unto thee, O LORD, and we shall be turned; renew our days as of old. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:21"},{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"22","sid":"LAM 5:22"},"But thou hast utterly rejected us; thou art very wroth against us. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"LAM 5:22"}]}]}
